Rast <rast2@hotmail.com> wrote:
>As far as I'm concerned, there are only two kinds of liches: those that can 
>teleport, and those that can't.  I dunno why the game divides them up into 
>four kinds.

There are four kinds, and each of the higher kinds has all the powers of
the ones before it (but more hit points, and a more powerful cold
attack, although the cold attack is mostly useless).

Liches (brown 'L'), who can destroy your armour, turn themselves
invisible, drain your strength, curse your possessions, stun you, haste
themselves, heal themselves, and cast psionic bolts at you, can touch you
to do cold damage, and are immune to cold, poison, and sleep.

Demiliches (red 'L'), who can aggravate the denizens of the dungeon
(although some brown 'L' will get a level boost and be able to do this,
too).

Master liches (purple 'L'), who can summon hordes (again, some red 'L'
can do this too due to level boosts), can use the tactics and strategy
module to teleport themselves in pursuit of various goals (which even
level-boosted red 'L' can't), and are additionally immune to fire.

Arch-liches (purple 'L'), who can kill you on the spot if you lack magic
resistance (in principle, one of the third kind might get enough of a
level boost to do this, but it's unlikely) and are additionally immune
to lightning.

Of course, as far as I'm concerned, there's only two kinds of lich: the
kind I haven't genocided yet and the kind I *have* genocided.

